      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This variation of the Ḥatsi Qaddish can be found in Seder Rav Amram as attested on fol. 6r of JTS MS 4074. The full JTS MS 4074 can be found digitized, here.</tei:p>
        <tei:p>David Hedegard transcribed three manuscript versions of Ḥatsi Qaddish in his dissertation on Seder R. Amram Gaon (Lindstedt, 1951). In his transcription, this source is labeled [ז] and in his translation, [S]. I have modifited Hedegard’s translation slightly by re-Hebraizing divine names.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_68681_notes"/>
